# Line endings, pinned.
#
# Every tracked text file in this repo is CRLF, including the shipped PowerShell, batch,
# markdown, and skill files. That is deliberate: the kit installs these files onto Windows
# machines and compares some of them by SHA-256, so the bytes on disk must match the bytes
# in the repo. Without this file, a contributor whose Git has core.autocrlf configured
# differently could commit LF versions, and a fresh clone would then install files that
# differ from the ones that were tested.
#
# text=auto is intentionally NOT used: it would let Git normalize on checkout and
# reintroduce exactly the drift this file exists to prevent.
#
# Binary assets are listed explicitly so they are never converted.

*.svg binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.exe binary

*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.psm1 text eol=crlf
*.toml text eol=crlf
*.md text eol=crlf
*.html text eol=crlf
*.json text eol=crlf
*.txt text eol=crlf
*.gitignore text eol=crlf
.gitattributes text eol=crlf
